    "content": "The U.S. stock market (NYSE and Nasdaq) opens for regular trading at 9:30 a.m. Eastern Time (ET), Monday through Friday. The market closes at 4:00 p.m. ET, and it is closed on weekends and federal holidays. Pre-market trading usually starts at 4:00 a.m. ET, and after-hours trading runs until 8:00 p.m. ET.Key Times & Details:Regular Trading Hours: 9:30 a.m. – 4:00 p.m. ET.Time Zone Conversions:Eastern: 9:30 a.m. - 4 p.m.Central: 8:30 a.m. - 3 p.m.Mountain: 7:30 a.m. - 2 p.m.Pacific: 6:30 a.m. - 1 p.m.Extended Hours: Pre-market starts as early as 4 a.m. ET, and after-hours lasts until 8 p.m. ET.Holidays: The market is closed on major holidays, such as New Year's Day, Memorial Day, and Christmas.Early Closures: On certain days, such as the day after Thanksgiving and Christmas Eve, the market closes early at 1:00 p.m. ET.If you are looking for specific market news or to set up pre-market trades, many investors start tracking activity during the 8:00 a.m. to 9:30 a.m. ET window before the opening bell.",
